WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.827 --> 00:00:07.427
In this video, you'll see how many students across your district have practiced each graduate attribute this year.

2
00:00:07.931 --> 00:00:20.921
Select Graduate Evidence in the menu. The page always shows the current school year. It counts students in every school in your district, and shows counts and percentages only. No student or teacher is named.

3
00:00:21.423 --> 00:00:33.993
Under By group, each row is a school, with its number of students and how many attributes those students have practiced. A school with very few students is combined with another, so no one can be picked out.

4
00:00:34.495 --> 00:00:47.385
Below that, each attribute shows how many students have practiced it. Dark means they finished an activity connected to it, and light means a related activity. It shows practice, not how well a student did.

5
00:00:47.887 --> 00:00:53.677
If no activity is connected to an attribute yet, the page says so instead of showing zero.

6
00:00:54.178 --> 00:00:57.698
To share this with your board, select Print this report.

7
00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:06.780
These connections are Fixer Nation's own mapping to New York's frameworks. Neither New York State nor CASEL has endorsed them.
